      "latin": "ānxius, ānxia, ānxium",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "classical",
      "gloss": "anxious, uneasy, troubled",
      "evidence": [
        "Cic. Tusc. 4.27; Cic. Fin. 2.55: <span lang=\"la\">ānxiō animō aut sollicitō esse</span> (Lewis &amp; Short)",
        "Andresian p. 36",
        "Traupman 272",
        "Traupman 392"
      ],
      "comment": "Cicero’s word for anxiety as a lasting cast of mind, against <span lang=\"la\">angī</span>, to be in distress for a moment (Tusc. 4.27). The vowel is long before <span lang=\"la\">-nx-</span>, which Lewis &amp; Short leaves unmarked."
    },
